{"text": "LANDRY & CASTILLE, L.L.C.\nATTORNEY WORK PRODUCT -- DEPOSITION SUMMARY\n\nCase:       ESTATE OF CLARENCE J. THIBODEAUX JR., through its administratrix\n            EARLINE THIBODEAUX, et al. v. BAYOU TECHE SURGICAL ASSOCIATES, APMC, et al.\nCourt:      15th Judicial District Court, Lafayette Parish, Louisiana\nDocket:     No. C-2025-4471, Div. K\nOur file:   LC-24-0933\nDeponent:   Anand Krishnamurthy, M.D. (defendant)\nTaken:      Thursday, July 9, 2026, 9:38 a.m. to 4:52 p.m.\nPlace:      Acadiana Court Reporters, Inc., 600 Jefferson Street, Suite 1150, Lafayette, LA 70501\nReporter:   Janelle Guidry, CCR No. 2011-0447\nAppearing:  Beau Landry and Theo Castille for plaintiffs;\n            Patricia Nwosu-Hebert, Dugas Nwosu-Hebert LLP, for Dr. Krishnamurthy and BTSA\nTranscript: 241 pages. Summary prepared 7/16/2026 by TC.\n\nBOTTOM LINE\nDr. Krishnamurthy concedes he did not obtain a critical view of safety before\nclipping, did not convert to open, and did not personally see the patient on\nPOD 2 despite two calls from nursing. He blames the delay on the hospitalist\nand on the family's refusal of blood. He was a poor witness after lunch. The\nalcohol-treatment history came in over objection and he was visibly rattled.\n\n1. BACKGROUND AND CREDENTIALS (pp. 6-41)\n\nBorn in Chennai; came to the United States in 1998; naturalized U.S. citizen since 2009\n(11:4-12). Medical school abroad, residency at a university program in\nShreveport. Louisiana license no. MD.204417; NPI 1740388215; DEA registration\nFK4471826 (14:2-15:9). Board certified in general surgery, recertified 2019.\nJoined Bayou Teche Surgical Associates, APMC in August 2012; became a shareholder in\n2016. Senior partner is Dr. Gerald Broussard, whom everyone calls \"Gerry\" (22:1).\n\nHe performs \"roughly 150 to 180\" laparoscopic cholecystectomies a year (CPT 47562).\nHe admitted one prior bile duct injury, in 2018, which was \"recognized on the\ntable and repaired\" (27:14-29:3). That claim, he agreed, was settled by his\ncarrier in 2019 for $350,000 without a panel opinion (30:6-22). Ms. Nwosu-Hebert\nobjected; instruction not to answer was withdrawn after we cited La. C.C.P. art. 1443.\n\nInsurance: Pelican Physicians Mutual Insurance Co., policy no. PPM-LA-0092817, limits\n$1 million per claim. He is a qualified provider under La. R.S. 40:1231.8, so\nthe cap applies. He does not know whether Pelican has reserved the claim (33:1-9).\n\nHealth and fitness for duty (34:12-41:20). Over a continuing objection he\ntestified that he completed a 90-day residential program for alcohol dependence in\nearly 2021 under a monitoring agreement with the state physicians' health program,\nthat the agreement ran five years, and that it was still in force on the date\nof surgery. He denies any relapse. He agreed that his privileges at\nOur Lady of the Bayou Medical Center were \"voluntarily restricted\" for eleven weeks in 2021.\nHe takes naltrexone 50 mg daily (39:7). He said random screens were all negative; we\nhave not seen them. FOLLOW UP: subpoena the monitoring file.\n\n2. THE PATIENT (pp. 42-67)\n\nClarence J. Thibodeaux Jr., known as \"Boo,\" DOB 04/02/1958, hospital MRN OLB-00381127,\nof 1187 Bayou Tortue Road, Youngsville, LA 70518. Retired after 31 years as a\nmachinist at Atchafalaya Pipe & Supply Co.; Army veteran. History of type 2 diabetes,\natrial fibrillation on apixaban, and BMI of 37 (Exhibit 7, H&P). The witness first\nsaw Mr. Thibodeaux in clinic on January 6, 2025 for symptomatic gallstones on referral\nfrom his PCP.\n\nThe witness knew from the intake sheet that Mr. Thibodeaux and his wife are\nJehovah's Witnesses and that he carried a signed refusal of blood products\n(48:3-49:17). He agreed the refusal covered whole blood and red cells but not\nalbumin or cell salvage, and that he \"did not get into those details\" at the\nconsent visit. He did not call the liaison committee at the St. Landry Parish Kingdom Hall\nalthough the family asked him to (51:2).\n\nConsent was signed January 20, 2025. Apixaban was held 48 hours. He does not recall\ndiscussing conversion to open or bile duct injury specifically; the form lists\nboth (53:10-56:1).\n\n3. THE OPERATION -- JANUARY 23, 2025 (pp. 68-121)\n\nSurgery at OLB main OR, room 6, in-room 7:42 a.m., incision 8:09, close 9:31.\nAssisted by a first-year PA whose name he could not recall. No cholangiogram:\n\"I do them selectively\" (74:8). He described \"a fair amount of inflammation\" in\nCalot's triangle and agreed that his operative note does not use the words\n\"critical view\" (79:1-81:15). He placed two clips on what he believed was the\ncystic duct and divided it. Shown the still images (Landry Exhibits 11-14), he\nagreed that the structure \"could be\" the common duct and that its diameter on\nimage 13 \"looks larger than I remembered\" (88:20-90:6).\n\nHe agreed with Dr. Howard Weiss's report that the injury is a Strasberg class E2\ntransection, but not that it was below the standard of care: \"it is a known\ncomplication\" (97:3). Asked why he did not convert or call Dr. Broussard, who\nwas operating next door: \"In hindsight I would have\" (101:12).\n\nEHR audit log (Exhibit 19). The operative note was created at 9:58 a.m. under\nuser ID akrishnamurthy2 from workstation OR6-WS02, IP 10.44.6.112, and was amended\nat 6:14 a.m. on 1/26/2025, after the transfer, from a remote session at\n198.51.100.23. The amendment added the sentence \"anatomy clearly identified.\"\nHe says he was \"cleaning up dictation\" from home (112:5-118:22). This is the\nbest material in the transcript.\n\n4. POST-OPERATIVE COURSE (pp. 122-198)\n\nDischarged home same day at 1:15 p.m. Returned to the ED the next evening,\nJanuary 24, with pain and vomiting; admitted to the hospitalist service under\nDr. Simone Fontenot-Reyes. Labs that night: WBC 19.4, total bilirubin 4.8,\nlactate 3.1 (Exhibit 22).\n\nNurse Tran (Kim-Ly Tran, RN) charted calls to the witness's cell, 337-555-0181, at\n10:52 p.m. and 2:17 a.m. He remembers one call, not two, and says he ordered a\nHIDA scan \"for the morning\" (131:4-134:9). His phone records (Exhibit 24) show\nboth calls connected, 3 min and 1 min. He was not on call; Gerry was. He did\nnot come in. He first examined the patient at about 11:30 a.m. on January 25,\nsome 26 hours after readmission (140:2).\n\nBy then the patient was septic, with a hemoglobin of 6.9. The family, through\nMrs. Thibodeaux and their daughter Monique Thibodeaux-Arceneaux, declined transfusion. The\nwitness testified that \"if they had let us give blood he would be alive\"\n(152:11). On cross by Mr. Landry he agreed that the bleeding followed the\nbile leak, that the leak followed the transection, and that no one offered\ncell salvage or erythropoietin (155:1-158:16). He conceded Dr. Fontenot-Reyes\nasked him twice for a surgical decision before ERCP was arranged.\n\nTransfer to a tertiary center in New Orleans was requested at 4:40 p.m. on\nthe 25th and accepted at 9:05 p.m.; the patient left by ground at 1:20 a.m.\nHe died on January 29, 2025 of biliary sepsis and multi-organ failure (death\ncertificate, Exhibit 31). He was 66.\n\nThe witness did not attend the funeral and has not spoken with the family.\nHe learned from Earline's pastor -- he corrected himself, \"her elder\" -- that\nthe decedent's mother, Odile Thibodeaux, who is 92, had been living with the\ncouple and depended on Clarence's pension (171:9). Monique now cares for her.\n\n5. DAMAGES-RELATED TESTIMONY (pp. 199-214)\n\nHe agreed the hospital bill at OLB was $84,219.57 and that the tertiary\ncenter billed $212,400 (Exhibits 33-34). He does not dispute funeral\nexpenses of $11,875.00. He has no opinion on lost pension income, which our\neconomist puts at about 19k a year.\n\n6. MISCELLANEOUS (pp. 215-241)\n\n- He reviewed his own notes, the Weiss report and \"some texts\" before testifying.\n  The texts are with Broussard on the night of the 24th. Not produced. We\n  demanded them on the record (217:3); Patricia agreed to \"look into it.\"\n- BTSA's tax ID appears on Exhibit 33 as 72-1408856; the billing address is\n  P.O. Box 53310, Lafayette, LA 70505-3310.\n- He has never been deposed under Rule 30(b)(6) and does not know who BTSA's\n  records custodian is.\n- Read and sign reserved. Errata due 30 days after receipt.\n\nTO DO (BL / TC)\n1. Motion to compel the Broussard texts and the monitoring file.\n2. Forensic image of the home computer; subpoena the ISP for 198.51.100.23.\n3. Depose Dr. Fontenot-Reyes and Ms. Tran before the panel submission deadline,\n   September 30, 2026.\n4. Ask Dr. Weiss to address cell salvage and the blood-refusal liaison issue.\n5. Send Mrs. T a short update; she prefers calls to (337) 555-0126 after 5.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "1,387 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Anand Krishnamurthy", "Beau Landry", "Theo Castille", "Patricia Nwosu-Hebert", "Dr. Gerald Broussard", "Clarence J. Thibodeaux Jr.", "Boo", "Mr. Thibodeaux", "akrishnamurthy2", "Howard Weiss", "Simone Fontenot-Reyes", "Kim-Ly Tran", "Gerry", "Mrs. Thibodeaux", "Monique Thibodeaux-Arceneaux", "Clarence", "Odile Thibodeaux", "Earline", "Patricia", "Broussard", "Weiss", "Dr. Fontenot-Reyes", "Ms. Tran", "Dr. Weiss", "Mrs. T"], "companies": ["LANDRY & CASTILLE, L.L.C.", "Bayou Teche Surgical Associates", "APMC", "Dugas Nwosu-Hebert LLP", "Bayou Teche Surgical Associates, APMC", "Louisiana", "MD.204417", "FK4471826", "Google", "Pelican Physicians Mutual Insurance Co.", "Atchafalaya Pipe & Supply Co.", "OLB", "New Orleans", "BTSA"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Shreveport", "Louisiana", "Lafayette Parish", "Acadiana Court Reporters", "Lafayette", "Chennai", "Bayou Tortue Road", " Youngsville", "LA 70518", "St. Landry Parish Kingdom Hall", "OLB main OR", "OR6-WS02", "New Orleans", "BL", "TC"], "health": ["diabetes", "atrial fibrillation", "apixaban", "BMI of 37", "gallstones", "naltrexone", "relapse", "conversion to open or bile duct injury", "inflammation", "WBC", "WBC 19.4", "lactate 3.1", "septic", "hemoglobin", "biliary sepsis", "multi-organ failure", "ERCP", "CPK", "transfusion", "erythropoietin"], "sensitive": ["EARLINE THIBODEAUX", "race or ethnicity", "religion", "political views or donations", "union membership", "immigration or citizenship status"], "names": ["Clarence J.", "Anand", "Gerald", "Theo", "Janelle", "Clarence", "Boo", "akrishnamurthy", "Simone Fontenot-Reyes", "Tran", "Mrs.", "Monique", "Odile", "Patricia", "Broussard", "Earline", "Dr."]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 5, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.10000000149011612, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 25, "text": "LANDRY & CASTILLE, L.L.C.", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "LANDRY & CASTILLE, L.L.C."}, {"start": 83, "end": 119, "text": "ESTATE OF CLARENCE J. THIBODEAUX JR.", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "ESTATE OF CLARENCE J. THIBODEAUX JR."}, {"start": 160, "end": 178, "text": "EARLINE THIBODEAUX", "kind": "sensitive", "source": "model", "canonical": "EARLINE THIBODEAUX"}, {"start": 190, "end": 227, "text": "BAYOU TECHE SURGICAL ASSOCIATES, APMC", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Bayou Teche Surgical Associates, APMC"}, {"start": 253, "end": 261, "text": "Judicial", "kind": "places", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "Judicial"}, {"start": 278, "end": 294, "text": "Lafayette Parish", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Lafayette Parish"}, {"start": 296, "end": 305, "text": "Louisiana", "